{"kind": "journal", "text": "Findings: panel shows strong cross-sectional long-horizon mean reversion (ret 60-250 all negative SR; ma 120-250 near +0.95 with a broad plateau confirmed across ret, ma, minr, maxr formulations) plus a distinct weekly echo in which returns from roughly days t-8 to t-5 predict positively (delay(ret(3),5) SR 1.23) with a coherent oscillation pattern (negative lobes at lags 0-5 and 10-15). The two engines are nearly orthogonal and a 1:1 cs_z blend reaches SR about 2.07; kurt(250) adds a small orthogonal kicker to 2.15. Blend SR stays 1.9-2.16 across weightings, reversal horizon sets, and rank vs z weighting, i.e. a parameter plateau rather than a lucky spike. Reporting three plateau variants that share the two validated engines and differ in reversal horizon set and the kurt add-on to hedge specification risk.", "ts": "2026-09-01T06:15:19.432571+00:00"}
{"kind": "report", "top3_chosen": ["add(add(cs_z(add(ma(120), ma(250))), cs_z(delay(ret(3), 5))), cs_z(kurt(250)))", "add(add(cs_z(add(ma(60), add(ma(120), ma(250)))), cs_z(delay(ret(3), 5))), cs_z(kurt(250)))", "add(cs_z(add(ma(120), ma(250))), cs_z(delay(ret(3), 5)))"], "chosen_sr_train": [2.147, 2.136, 2.068], "rationale": "All three combine the two independently validated engines: long-horizon cross-sectional mean reversion (ma 120-250, plateau confirmed across ret, ma, minr and maxr formulations at horizons 60-250) and a weekly return echo (returns from days t-8 to t-5 predict positively, with a coherent oscillating lag profile). The engines are nearly orthogonal, and blend train SR sits on a broad 1.9-2.16 plateau across weightings, horizon sets and rank vs z normalization, which argues the edge is structural rather than a selection artifact. Variants differ in reversal horizon set and a small kurt(250) add-on to hedge specification risk.", "n_batches_used": 6, "ts": "2026-09-01T06:15:26.133284+00:00"}
